Audit of Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS: 34 controls

STATUS   ID       SEVERITY  CONTROL
FAIL     FW-001   medium    Incoming traffic denied by default
         no firewall rules filter incoming traffic
         Without it, any service listening on all addresses, such as a database
         left at its defaults, is reachable from the internet. A firewall at
         your provider also protects the server, but this check cannot see it.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module firewall.inbound
FAIL     NET-005  medium    IPv4 ICMP redirects not accepted
         ICMP redirects are accepted on new interfaces (default) and ens3:
         accept_redirects 1 in all and on each, forwarding 0 on each
         Accepted ICMP redirects change the server's routes, so a forged
         redirect can send its traffic through another machine on the local
         network.
         fix: not automated yet
FAIL     SSH-001  medium    Root login disabled
         permitrootlogin is prohibit-password, expected no
         Root is the one account name every scanner tries, and its actions are
         not tied to a person. Log in as a named user and use sudo.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module ssh.server
FAIL     UPD-001  medium    Security updates installed automatically
         unattended-upgrades is not installed
         Attackers scan for a flaw soon after its fix is published. Unattended
         upgrades install security fixes on their own, so a server nobody logs
         into still gets them.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module updates.auto
FAIL     NET-007  low       Multipath TCP disabled
         net.mptcp.enabled is 1, expected 0
         Multipath TCP is rarely needed on a server and adds kernel code to
         every TCP handshake. Go 1.24+ programs such as Caddy, Docker and
         tailscaled open MPTCP listeners by default, so a flaw in it is
         reachable from the network without any setup.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module kernel.sysctl
FAIL     SSH-005  low       X11 forwarding disabled
         x11forwarding is yes, expected no
         A server has no use for graphical apps, and a forwarded display lets
         the server reach into your desktop session.
         fix: sudo vps-ready apply --module ssh.server

25 passed, 6 failed (4 medium, 2 low), 0 unknown, 3 skipped
Skipped: there is no VPN interface (WireGuard or tailscale0) and no `ssh_via` rule.
Skipped: /etc/wireguard does not exist.
Skipped: Docker is not installed.
vps-ready can fix 5 of the 6 (FW-001, SSH-001, UPD-001, NET-007, SSH-005): run
`sudo vps-ready plan --module firewall.inbound --module ssh.server --module
updates.auto --module kernel.sysctl`.
The other one needs a manual fix for now; it says so above.
Run `vps-ready audit --all` to list the 25 passing controls too.
